MiniDSH is an independent educational and engineering project inspired by
DeepSeek Harness (https://github.com/deepseek-ai/deepseek-harness, MIT
License, Copyright DeepSeek). It is not an official DeepSeek project and is
not affiliated with or endorsed by DeepSeek.

The code is implemented independently. Where a contract, profile or wording
is adapted from DeepSeek Harness -- for example the bubblewrap confinement
profile and the shape of the JSON-RPC client protocol -- the source is
credited in the adjacent comment. The Cordis paper
(https://github.com/cordiverse/paper) is the source of the two composability
properties the kernel is built around.

The browser client (src/app/web) adapts two pieces of DeepSeek Harness's
web client, at commit 2e39e70496aa02986ca6a820c5d497e816b69d7e: the line
icon artwork in icons.js (from packages/client/ui-primitives/src/icons/
artwork.ts, converted to element data and renamed), and the values of its
design tokens in style.css (the neutral ramp, hairlines, elevation, radii,
type scale and diff and syntax colours, from packages/client/ui-theme).
MiniDSH's mark and accent colour are its own; no DeepSeek brand artwork is
used. That material is used under DeepSeek Harness's licence:

